@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+| ID | Behavior | Spec reference | How to verify | Code | Evidence | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| I-1 | Each ordered step has stable identity, era, title, caption and scene state; displayed numbering follows its position. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Scene step model” | Component test renders reordered steps and checks metadata and derived numbering. | `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx`, `types.ts` | `derives-numbering-final.log`: derives numbering and shows reordered metadata | verified |
+| I-2 | Strongly typed grouped payloads pass through the presentation boundary without casts. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Scene step model” | Type-check a typed grouped-scene fixture with `npm run build`. | `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx`, `src/presentations/how-to-make-a-presentation/Talk.tsx` | `resolve-build.log`: npm run build type-checks typed grouped steps without casts | verified |
+| I-3 | Stable entities morph between adjacent steps; newcomers enter after continuing entities settle, and departing entities exit. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Stable entities morph across steps” | Inspect motion configuration and identity usage; component tests check shared identities, entry timing and exit configuration. | `src/presentation-kit/nodes/index.tsx`, `constants.ts` | `resolve-targeted.log`: keeps a continuing entity while a newcomer enters and exits; `resolve-connector-retest.log`: animates the conversation connector in and out; `resolve-kit-inspection.txt`; `resolve-scene-inspection.txt` | verified |
+| I-4 | Adjacent steps sharing a group and scene update one mounted instance; continuing entities avoid newcomer fades and intentional stacking is preserved. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Persistent grouped scenes” | Component test tracks scene mounts and payload updates; inspect sample composition and transition configuration. | `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx`, `src/presentations/how-to-make-a-presentation/Talk.tsx` | `resolve-targeted.log`: keeps grouped scene mounted while payload changes; `resolve-scene-inspection.txt` | verified |
+| I-5 | Kit primitives and chrome expose stable styling hooks and class/style hooks for coordinates, without visual defaults or a required styling framework; raw motion elements can use stable identities. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Style ownership boundary” | Component tests check hooks and forwarded properties; inspect kit and dependencies for styling ownership. INT-001 checks materialized scaffold neutrality and kit parity. | `src/presentation-kit/`, `skills/presentation/templates/bootstrap/` | `resolve-fixture-final.log`: INT-001 neutrality of scaffold source and kit parity; `resolve-targeted.log`: primitive hooks; `resolve-kit-inspection.txt` | verified |
+| I-6 | Default bottom-right attribution links to the and-scene GitHub repository, has a styling hook, and no default top-left brand; host branding is opt-in. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Kit attribution” | Component test checks default link, placement hook and optional branding. | `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx` | `defaults-attribution-final.log` and `exposes-node-final.log`: default link, placement, no default brand and opt-in brand | verified |
+| I-7 | Present mode shows marker and title without caption, table of contents or prev/next; browse mode shows title, caption, wide-screen contents, controls and progress; initial mode is configurable and toggling preserves position. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Present and browse modes” | Component tests cover both modes, initial mode, wide-screen contents and preserved step on toggle. | `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx`, `src/presentations/how-to-make-a-presentation/style.css` | `resolve-targeted.log`: switches modes without losing position and starts in present mode; `resolve-scene-inspection.txt` | verified |
+| I-8 | Keyboard navigation supports Right, Space and PageDown forward, Left and PageUp backward, and does not hijack focused controls; horizontal swipes navigate in the expected direction. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Step navigation” | Navigation hook/component tests exercise keys, focused controls and both swipe directions. | `src/presentation-kit/usePresentationNav.ts` | `navigates-keys-final.log`: navigates keys, swipes, direct jumps and preserves control keys | verified |
+| I-9 | Progress controls jump to their step, contents entries jump to the first step of their era, and active controls expose semantic current state and stable active hooks. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Step navigation” | Component tests exercise direct jumps and active semantics and hooks. | `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx` | `navigates-keys-final.log`: direct jumps and active semantics | verified |
+| I-10 | Navigation clamps at the first and last steps without wrapping. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Boundary behavior” | Navigation unit tests exercise both boundaries. | `src/presentation-kit/usePresentationNav.ts` | `clamps-both-final.log`: clamps both ends | verified |
+| I-11 | The default 880 × 380 canvas scales uniformly to fit on resize, without internal reflow, using mode-specific geometry. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Fixed-canvas fit scaling” | Fit-scale unit tests cover dimensions, resize and both modes; inspect stage transform and fixed-canvas layout. | `src/presentation-kit/useFitScale.ts`, `constants.ts`, `Presentation.tsx` | `resolve-targeted.log`: updates the fixed canvas transform on viewport resize; `resolve-kit-inspection.txt` | verified |
+| I-12 | The skill asks for missing topic, style and each step’s content and visual description one question at a time; it accepts partial detail, can proceed with complete input and may use selective ASCII mockups. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Interactive requirement gathering” | Inspect skill instructions for each gathering path and optional mockups. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md` | `resolve-skill-inspection.txt`: gathering, partial detail and mockup instructions | verified |
+| I-13 | The skill detects the three anchors by contract, fully scaffolds an unscaffolded target, skips existing anchors, and adds only missing anchors and dependencies for partial scaffolds. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Self-bootstrapping scaffold” | Inspect skill instructions for detection and preservation; INT-001 materializes and checks the complete bootstrap. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md`, `templates/bootstrap` | `resolve-skill-inspection.txt`: anchor detection and partial scaffolding; `resolve-fixture-final.log`: INT-001 neutral materialized bootstrap | verified |
+| I-14 | Scaffold target resolution uses the standalone root or a self-contained monorepo `presentations/` app, and requires confirmation of the target before scaffolding a non-empty project missing kit or index. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Self-bootstrapping scaffold” | Inspect skill instructions for target resolution and confirmation. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md` | `resolve-skill-inspection.txt`: target resolution and confirmation instructions | verified |
+| I-15 | Templates resolve relative to the skill file; scaffold installs the complete runtime, build, lint and browser verification dependencies without imposing visual defaults or a styling framework. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Self-bootstrapping scaffold” | Inspect skill and template files; INT-001 checks lookup, installed dependencies, build and neutrality outside the source repository. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md`, `templates/bootstrap` | `resolve-skill-inspection.txt` and `template-path-inspection.txt`: skill-relative lookup; `lead-ruling.txt`; `resolve-fixture-final.log`: INT-001 dependencies, neutrality and materialized bootstrap | verified |
+| I-16 | A new presentation has its own folder, route and registry entry, uses presentation- or host-owned styling with plain CSS by default, and preserves existing presentations and routes. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Create a new presentation” | Inspect skill instructions and templates; unit test explicit registry and route resolution for multiple entries. | `src/main.tsx`, `src/presentations/resolve.ts`, `skills/presentation/` | `resolve-targeted.log`: resolves multiple registered presentation routes; `resolve-skill-inspection.txt` | verified |
+| I-17 | An ambiguous modification lists candidates and asks for a target before edits; a clear target receives only requested, scoped changes without repeating creation questions. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Modify an existing presentation” | Inspect skill instructions for ambiguity and scoped modification. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md` | `resolve-skill-inspection.txt`: ambiguous and scoped modification instructions | verified |
+| I-18 | Before success, the skill builds, renders at least the first step without errors, inspects first, last and dense/key steps and narrow views when sensitive, and fixes and rechecks failures. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Self-verify before reporting completion” | Inspect skill instructions for verification, visual inspection and repair loop. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md` | `resolve-skill-inspection.txt`: build, render, visual check and repair instructions | verified |
+| I-19 | Generated presentations have per-step captions, next/previous navigation and an evolving scene; visual checks cover fixed-canvas fit, readable intentional overlaps and chrome collisions. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Generated presentation quality bar” | Inspect skill instructions and presentation templates; component tests cover captions and navigation. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md`, `skills/presentation/templates/presentation/Talk.tsx.template` | `resolve-targeted.log`: continuing entity enters and exits, captions and navigation; `resolve-skill-inspection.txt`: grouped child presence and template | verified |
+| I-20 | Screenshot work prefers the project-local helper, otherwise uses a temporary helper under the project root; warnings are reviewed and accidental collisions and indistinct chrome fixed, with only readable intentional overlap marked. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Generated presentation quality bar” | Inspect skill instructions for helper location, warning review and repair. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md` | `resolve-skill-inspection.txt`: helper location and visual warning review | verified |
+| I-21 | Active chrome and attribution are visibly styled by presentation or host CSS while the kit remains style-neutral. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Generated presentation quality bar” | Inspect skill instructions and sample-owned CSS; INT-002 checks diagnostic detection of indistinct chrome and unpolished attribution. | `src/presentations/how-to-make-a-presentation/style.css`, `skills/presentation/SKILL.md` | `resolve-skill-inspection.txt` and `resolve-scene-inspection.txt`: local active and attribution styling; `resolve-fixture-final.log`: INT-002 chrome diagnostics | verified |
+| I-22 | Verification builds the whole application and reports an actionable nonzero failure for type or build errors. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Build verification”; “Pass/fail reporting” | E2E-001 checks successful whole-app build; E2E-002 injects a build failure and checks phase and exit status. | `scripts/verify.mjs` | `resolve-targeted.log`: E2E-001 production verification and E2E-002 build-failure case | verified |
+| I-23 | The registered, reachable reference sample has the nine specified eras, titles, captions and accumulating scene intents in order, ending in the self-reference reveal. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Committed reference sample” | E2E-001 checks registration, reachability and ordered titles/captions; inspect sample scenes against all nine normative intents and accumulation. | `src/presentations/how-to-make-a-presentation/Talk.tsx` | `resolve-connector-retest.log`: connector entry/exit and conversation and depth relationships; `resolve-targeted.log`: E2E-001 production verification; `resolve-scene-inspection.txt`: all nine scene intents | verified |
+| I-24 | Verification fails for an absent or malformed sample, including out-of-order content. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Committed reference sample” | E2E-002 injects missing and out-of-order sample faults and checks nonzero, phase-specific output. | `scripts/verify.mjs` | `resolve-targeted.log`: E2E-002 reports missing sample and wrong sample order after swapping complete steps | verified |
+| I-25 | Production verification uses IPv4 loopback for preview, readiness and browser URLs, enumerates all steps through public hooks, and reports clear success. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Render verification”; “Pass/fail reporting” | E2E-001 runs `npm run verify` and checks host, all step indices and success output. | `scripts/browser-utils.mjs`, `scripts/verify.mjs` | `resolve-targeted.log`: E2E-001 production verification; `ipv4-final-inspection.txt`: loopback preview, readiness and route URLs | verified |
+| I-26 | Console errors, uncaught page errors, render errors and failed transitions fail verification with the offending step; preview processes are cleaned up on failure. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Render verification”; “Pass/fail reporting” | E2E-002 injects browser and transition faults and checks nonzero output, step identification and subprocess cleanup. | `scripts/verify.mjs`, `scripts/browser-utils.mjs` | `resolve-targeted.log`: E2E-002 console, page, first-step and later render errors and failed transition, with preview cleanup | verified |
+| I-27 | The project-local helper captures each registered presentation step at a standard desktop viewport in a predictable local directory after the configured animation settle interval. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Visual inspection artifacts” | INT-002 checks screenshot count, paths and settle timing using a controlled presentation. | `scripts/inspect-presentation.mjs` | `resolve-fixture-final.log`: INT-002 checks per-capture active index, settle timing, distinct images and stalled-transition failure | verified |
+| I-28 | The helper warns with step and element details for unmarked visible text/chrome collisions and exempts explicitly marked allowed-overlap subtrees. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Visual inspection artifacts” | INT-002 checks an unmarked collision and an explicitly allowed overlap. | `scripts/inspect-presentation.mjs` | `resolve-fixture-final.log`: INT-002 detects direct div text collision and exempts marked overlap | verified |
+| I-29 | The helper emits advisory warnings for indistinct active progress or contents controls and missing, undersized or browser-default attribution, pointing to its styling hook. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Visual inspection artifacts” | INT-002 checks active-navigation and attribution diagnostics and their advisory output. | `scripts/inspect-presentation.mjs` | `resolve-fixture-final.log`: INT-002 detects foreground-only progress, indistinct contents and attribution defects | verified |
